The cache has a minimum TTL of 60 seconds. Even when the server returns a shorter TTL (1 second in this test), the client enforces a minimum of 60 seconds. In this test with a 2 second wait, the cache was still valid so no new network call was made. For the cache to actually expire and trigger a new fetch, you would need to wait at least 60 seconds.

